Mothers, ghosts, demons, and Brahma-Rakshasas were driven away. Prithagvidhani prayukt pinaakyastrani sharangine. With all his might, he struck down the Sharanga-bearing one, astonished. 12. Meaning of the word

Separate—of various types; Prayanka—attached; Pinaki—Shiva with the trident; Astraani—weapons; Sharangine—
Sharanga, the bow-wielder, against Krishna; Prati-astraiha—by opposing weapons; Shamayam Aas—calmed down; Sharanga-Paniha—Sharanga
bow-wielder; Avisitah—without even a little surprise. Shiva, the trident-bearing one, and Krishna, the archer, wielded numerous weapons against each other. But Krishna
was not disturbed even a bit—He neutralized all these weapons with appropriate counterweapons.
